- e_Plx (error in parallax): Large errors reduce reliability of distance and thus of absolute magnitude estimates.
- B-V (color index): Giants tend to have specific color indices depending on their spectral type; generally, giants are cooler and redder (higher B-V) than dwarfs of the same spectral class.
- SpType (spectral type): Luminosity class in SpType (e.g., III for giants, V for dwarfs) directly indicates if a star is giant or not.
- Amag (absolute magnitude): Giants have brighter absolute magnitudes (lower or negative Amag) than dwarfs of the same spectral type.

